  "scopeNotes": [
    "Availability lifecycle begins with explicit preexisting hub, queue, DA-parameter and correction-lock genesis fixtures; all attestation and availability state is produced by evaluated ledger transactions.",
    "The maximum 64 MiB commitment scenario fully publishes one 300-chunk tranche, partially publishes the second, settles all 16 tranches and times out with queue removal. It does not publish all 64 MiB.",
    "The separate 4 MiB + 1 byte scenario publishes and reassembles all 301 chunks across two tranches, settles both, and closes.",
    "Scenario deployment identities are rederived in each test with generated public actor identities. Rerun current-blueprint tests for release acceptance; this saved summary is not itself a release gate.",
    "Operational challenger commands, watcher/indexer integration, recovery and live Preprod acceptance remain separate work."
